  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Comprehensive Sexuality Education (CSE) to Prevent Violence in rural Madagascar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PJL aims to partner with the What Works 2 Research consortium to test and build upon a government adaptation of our CSE intervention to combat violence in new, very rural settings where little experience exists. This action-oriented research will 1) fill gaps in global knowledge on how widespread in-school CSE can work to prevent different forms of violence for the most marginalized groups in LICs, and 2) support PJL as a nationally recognized actor to inform program and policy solutions to prevent violence at scale.</narrative>
  </description>
